# Pin the CHECKOUT FORM of these text types to LF, independent of any clone's own core.autocrlf.
# Without this, a machine with core.autocrlf=true (the SYSTEM default on this machine) checks
# text files out with CRLF on a fresh clone, even though every blob in this repo is already
# LF-only (autocrlf normalizes on commit, not on checkout). tests/figure-derive.js byte-compares
# a generator's LF output against the checked-out fixture SVG; a CRLF checkout makes that compare
# fail for a reason that has nothing to do with what the gate exists to guard, and the failure
# message is actively misleading (it reads as genSvg nondeterminism). This fixes the checkout
# form, not the comparison -- normalizing bytes inside a verifier would hide real corruption
# along with this one.
*.svg text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
